{"kind":"changes-requested","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact head 14c4a3cbaef1d93d0a5e3cb3ba8408075351a011 (request/custody-lost-update-final), reviewed in a clean checkout of that exact commit. The five gaps are genuinely closed in code, and planner request #8762's conditions 1–4 hold in substance: reload-and-merge under flock/LockFileEx with per-caller declared conflict rules (never last-writer-wins); configMu-guarded Config view with zero uncovered w.Config reads outside init and SaveConfig fully removed; CreateConfig rechecks absence inside the exclusive lock at initHosted, AttachConfig and host.Init, with UpdateConfig writing through unexported writeConfigFile and no recursive locking; O_EXCL key creation in generateActor so a losing same-name AddActor never reaches a durable roster act nor overwrites winner bytes, refusing different custody at merge. My own mutation spot-check (throwaway worktree, removed after): deleting UpdateConfig's reload makes TestUpdateConfigPreservesConcurrentCustody and TestStaleWorkspaceSavePreservesConcurrentCustody fail by name — the two-openings regression is genuinely mutation-sensitive.\n\nBut the required gate go test -count=1 ./... is deterministically RED at this exact head, which both governing requests demand green and both reporting artifacts claim clean. Reproduced on repeated runs, four failures in three packages:\n\n(1) internal/apphost TestCreateConfigCollisionSerialisesCreators can never pass: genesis(i)=sha1ID('A'+i) gives creators 6–7 the strings \"GGGG…\"…\"HHHH…\", not hex, so pre-lock Validate refuses \"invalid genesis object id\" instead of the asserted \"already exists\". Fixture bug in new test code; alone it disproves the artifacts' gate claim.\n(2) cmd/gs TestAttachRejectsSpentIdempotencyReplayAfterLocalFrontierLoss: an equal-depth sibling audit now refuses via the rollback rule before ancestry is consulted, so the error lacks the pinned \"non-descendant verified frontier\". The refusal itself is exactly what five-gap condition (1) asks for; the older pin was left unupdated.\n(3) internal/app TestAcceptSnapshotGuardsPreserveColdProjection/rewind_then_sibling_advance_is_refused: same class — pinned text \"shorter than previously verified\" is no longer produced; behaviour still refuses correctly.\n(4) internal/app TestVerifiedFrontierPersistenceIsPassiveWhenUnchangedAndFailClosedWhenAdvancing is a real semantic regression against a standing pin, not just wording: passive-when-unchanged required Snapshot/Verify to succeed with an unusable MetaDir; UpdateConfig must now take the lock and load before it can decide anything, so an unchanged audit hard-fails (ENOTDIR opening .config.lock) where main succeeds passively. app_test.go is untouched by this branch, so neither pin nor contract change was recorded.\n\nREQUIRED CHANGES: (a) fix the collision-test genesis fixture to valid hex ids; (b) update the two refusal-wording pins to the new rule-table messages, or keep the old wording deliberately; (c) resolve passive-when-unchanged explicitly — deciding from locked disk cannot stay passive when storage is unreadable, so either restore a narrowly safe passivity or change the pin and say the contract moved, in the open; (d) rerun the full gates (gofmt -l empty; go vet ./...; go test -count=1 ./...; go test -race ./...; git diff --check; GOOS=windows go build ./...) at a new exact head and republish successor artifacts at internal/apphost and internal/app — the current artifacts' stated gate results are inaccurate for this head.\n\nARCHITECTURE: affected layers per docs/reference/architecture.md are 4 Application host binding (internal/apphost configuration custody and locking) and 5 Application profile and interpreter (internal/app Workspace view and frontier witness). Their contracts as written are preserved by the code; no layer-page edit is required; but conclusion (4) above is a behavioural contract of the app layer changed silently, which must be either reverted or recorded with the pin.\n\nSECURITY: examined trust boundaries around local custody. flock (unix) / LockFileEx (windows) is held across the entire load-modify-store, closing the load→store TOCTOU; .config.lock is created 0600 inside metaDir (.git/gitseq), sits beside the file it guards, is never renamed, and the kernel releases it on process death; O_EXCL reservation means no recorded fingerprint can point at a losing call's private bytes; platforms without advisory locks refuse every locked operation loudly rather than pretend fail-closed coverage, with the refusal pinned in a correctly tagged test file; no key material appears in errors or logs. Two residual notes, neither a defect blocking this verdict class: AttachConfig routes through CreateConfig, so read-only attachment also becomes impossible on unsupported platforms — worth one sentence in that platform note; a creator whose roster act or adoption fails after winning O_EXCL leaves an orphaned 0600 key file (pre-existing shape, never pointed at by any recorded actor).\n\nSIMPLIFICATION: mergeVerifiedFrontier's rule table, cloneConfig and the guarded view are minimal and each maps to a named condition; nothing to cut without weakening conditions. Optional: folding post-reservation key cleanup into AddActor's failure paths would remove the orphaned-file note above.\n\nFILING NOTE: no durable exact-head review request addressed to me stands for this chain — ox-builder's #8853 condition to file one to a different actor is unmet as filed, and my only earlier promise on this chain (612e75e621f9) was judged ineffective because its basis addresses ox-builder — so gs review's promise check cannot be satisfied honestly and this verdict is hand-filed resting on the two artifacts it judges, per AGENTS.md step 4. Codex, as requester of #8853 (and steward of #8762's conditions alongside planner), ratifies from here.","body":{"conclusion_architecture":"Layers 4 (Application host binding, internal/apphost) and 5 (Application profile and interpreter, internal/app): contracts preserved in code, no architecture.md change required; but one pinned app-layer contract (passive witness when unchanged) changed silently.","conclusion_security":"Lock covers whole RMW closing TOCTOU; .config.lock 0600 inside .git/gitseq, never renamed, crash-safe; O_EXCL key custody; loud unsupported-platform refusal with correctly tagged test; no secrets in logs/errors. Residual non-blockers noted in text.","conclusion_simplification":"Rule table and cloneConfig are minimal, nothing to cut; optional orphaned-key cleanup note in text.","head":"14c4a3cbaef1d93d0a5e3cb3ba8408075351a011","review_request_gap":"No durable exact-head review request addressed to ox-checker stands for this head (an #8853 condition); verdict therefore hand-filed resting on the artifacts it names, per AGENTS.md step 4.","verdict":"changes-requested"}}